for Applications: Llama 3.1 Impact Grants\nL113: \nL114: We’re excited to begin accepting applications for the Llama 3.1 Impact Grants, the next iteration of a larger portfolio of work to support organizations as they pursue their ideas for how Llama can be used to address social challenges in their communities.\nL115: \nL116: August 05, 2024\nL117: \nL118: cite25†Learn More L119: \nL120: Blog\nL121: \nL122: September 25, 2024\nL123: \nL124: #### Open Source\nL125: #### Connect 2024: The responsible approach we’re taking to generative AI\nL126: \nL127: With the rapidly evolving AI landscape, we recognize the importance of sharing our responsibility and safety approach with everyone.\nL128: \nL129: September 25, 2024\nL130: \nL131: cite26†Learn More L132: \nL133: Blog\nL134: \nL135: September 25, 2024\nL136: \nL137: #### Developer Tools\nL138: \nL139: #### Open Source\nL140: #### Llama 3.2: Revolutionizing edge AI and vision with open, customizable models\nL141: \nL142: Today, we’re releasing Llama 3.2, which includes small and medium-sized vision LLMs, and lightweight, text-only models that fit onto edge and mobile devices.\nL143: \nL144: September 25, 2024\nL145: \nL146: cite27†Learn More L147: \nL148: Blog\nL149: \nL150: April 29, 2025\nL151: \nL152: #### Developer Tools\nL153: \nL154: #### Open Source\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQwen (https://qwenlm.github.io/)\nciteturn4848view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://qwenlm.github.io/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 36\n"
